NOTICE

This project uses the following third-party models and corpora.

Built with Meta Llama 3

Llama 3 8B (`llama3:8b`, served locally through Ollama) is used as a weak-supervision
labeller in this project (see `accord/differential/run_multillm_replication.py`,
and `accord/prevalence_replication/run_prevalence_sweep.py`). Use of Llama 3 is subject to the Meta
Llama 3 Community License; the attribution above is included per section 1.b of that
license.

Apache License 2.0 models

The following models are also used locally through Ollama, as comparison/replication
models alongside Llama 3, and are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  - Mistral 7B v0.3
  - Granite 3.3 8B (`granite3.3:8b`)
  - Qwen3 8B (`qwen3:8b`)

MIT-licensed encoder

PubMedBERT / BiomedNLP-BiomedBERT
(`microsoft/BiomedNLP-BiomedBERT-base-uncased-abstract-fulltext`), used as a pretrained
encoder baseline (see `accord/control/model.py`), is
distributed by Microsoft under the MIT License.

Label-free baseline

RoBERTa large fine-tuned on MNLI (`roberta-large-mnli`), run locally as a label-free
inference baseline (see `accord/differential/nli_baseline.py`), is used under the terms
of its model card.

Public benchmark and survey data used by the public control experiments:
- SNLI, the Stanford Natural Language Inference corpus (Bowman et al., 2015), Stanford NLP Group.
- AG News topic classification data (Zhang, Zhao and LeCun, 2015), derived from the AG corpus of news articles.
- American Community Survey Public Use Microdata Sample (PUMS), U.S. Census Bureau.
Each is used under the terms published by its provider. This repository commits only row indices, labels,
hashes, model scores and aggregate statistics derived from them, not the corpus text.
